# The input directory is the repo root, so the repo's own prose would otherwise
# be published as pages. .gitignore already covers scratch/ and node_modules/.
docs

# Every root markdown, not a list of the ones that exist today: CLAUDE.md and
# README.md were named individually, so a new one published silently. Verified
# by dropping probe-doc.md at the root and finding dist/probe-doc.html.
/*.md

# Eleventy crawls dot-directories, and .claude/ is neither gitignored nor
# ignored here, so the first agents/*.md or skills/*.md that lands in this repo
# would be rendered and published at /.claude/agents/<name>.html.
#
# Local nginx cannot show you this: docker/nginx.conf returns 404 for anything
# matching /\., so the dev container hides precisely the files Pages would
# serve. Verified by dropping .probe/x.md at the root and finding
# dist/.probe/x.html in the build.
#
# Wildcarded rather than naming .claude, so the next tool that drops a
# dot-directory here is covered without anyone remembering.
.*/
